{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And all the souls.</b> In many places in Scripture we find that it calls the human body a נפש, as in what is written (Leviticus 4:2): ״נפש כי תחטא״ — 'when a soul sins' — which refers to the human body, for sin does not come from the side of the soul. So too here, the intent of נפש is the body. Therefore it says: 'the ones who came out of Jacob's thigh, seventy souls' — and Joseph was already in Egypt, included with Joseph who was in Egypt. And it is known that he was in Egypt only because the future redemption will be modeled on the redemption from Egypt; therefore it hints that at the beginning of the first exile they were seventy souls, and at the end, in the last exile, they are destined to inherit seventy nations. This is the meaning of 'and Joseph was in Egypt' — it mentioned Joseph last, to hint at Messiah son of Joseph, who is destined to come at the end to redeem Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:26.667356228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}